! **A force in the noncollinear regime**, on the cheapest cell that has one.
!
! `h-chain-90deg.in`'s four-site hydrogen chain -- each atom's moment turned 90
! degrees from the one before, so the magnetization is genuinely a vector field
! and `nspin_mag = 4` -- with the second atom pushed 0.02 of the cell along z.
! That is 0.4 bohr on a 20-bohr cell and it leaves the chain unevenly spaced, so
! every atom has a force along z and nothing along x or y.
!
! Norm-conserving, so `S` is the identity and the force is pure
! Hellmann-Feynman: what it tests is the *spinor* nonlocal quadratic form with
! `dvan_so` (P46), not the augmentation charge -- `bi2-soc-force.in` is the case
! that adds that.
!
! `nosym` and one shifted k-point are inherited from the undisplaced file and
! are deliberate: the comparison is then between two codes summing the same
! Brillouin-zone sample, with no symmetrisation of a vector on either side. The
! wedge-against-full-grid check lives in `bi2-soc-force.in`, which has symmetry.
!
! conv_thr is 1e-11 for `si2-nc-force.in`'s reason: QE's printed force carries
! `force_corr`, which corrects a density that stopped short of the fixed point
! and has no counterpart in a force obtained by differentiating the energy *at*
! the fixed point.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
    tprnfor = .true.
    tstress = .true.
    verbosity = 'high'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 6, celldm(1) = 12.0, celldm(3) = 1.66666666666667,
    nat = 4, ntyp = 4,
    ecutwfc = 25.0,
    occupations = 'smearing', smearing = 'gaussian', degauss = 0.10
    noncolin = .true.
    nosym = .true.
    starting_magnetization(1) = 0.6, angle1(1) = 90.0, angle2(1) =   0.0
    starting_magnetization(2) = 0.6, angle1(2) = 90.0, angle2(2) =  90.0
    starting_magnetization(3) = 0.6, angle1(3) = 90.0, angle2(3) = 180.0
    starting_magnetization(4) = 0.6, angle1(4) = 90.0, angle2(4) = 270.0
    nbnd = 24
 /
 &electrons
    mixing_beta = 0.3
    conv_thr = 1.0d-11
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 H1  1.008  H.pz-vbc.UPF
 H2  1.008  H.pz-vbc.UPF
 H3  1.008  H.pz-vbc.UPF
 H4  1.008  H.pz-vbc.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (crystal)
 H1 0.0 0.0 0.00
 H2 0.0 0.0 0.27
 H3 0.0 0.0 0.50
 H4 0.0 0.0 0.75
K_POINTS {automatic}
 1 1 1 0 0 1
